<title>ROMANIA: Clinton leaves Romania for Denmark.</title>
<headline>Clinton leaves Romania for Denmark.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. President Bill Clinton left Romania on Friday after an eight-hour visit during which he told Romanians they stood a good chance of entering NATO in a subsequent wave of expansion if they pursued reforms.</p>
<p>A Romanian defence official said Clinton left Bucharest's Otopeni airport aboard Air Force One at 8.35 p.m. (1735 GMT) for Copenhagen, where he is to make a brief visit before returning to the United States.</p>
</text>
